  "definition": "Retainage on Construction Contracts",
  "effectiveDate": "2022-12-20",
  "historyNote": "(See Revision Notes #1-#3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 500) #10984, eff 12-1-15; ss by #13511, eff 12-20-22 (formerly Env-Wq 507.11)",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Wq 507.12",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 507.12 Retainage on Construction Contracts",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 507.12 Retainage on Construction Contracts.\n\n(a) The recipient shall withhold 10% of all partial payments as retainage until 50% of the project is complete.\n\n(b) After the project is 50% complete, no additional retainage shall be withheld from any partial payments.\n\n(c) Upon substantial or final completion of the project, the recipient shall reduce the retainage to 2%. The final 2% retainage shall be held during the one-year warranty period and released only after the recipient has accepted the project.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1-#3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 500) #10984, eff 12-1-15; ss by #13511, eff 12-20-22 (formerly Env-Wq 507.11)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq500.html"
